                <invention-title lang="de">VORRICHTUNG UND VERFAHREN ZUR AUSFÜHRUNG EINES DIREKTZUGRIFFS IN EINEM DRAHTLOSKOMMUNIKATIONSSYSTEM</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">APPAREIL ET PROCÉDÉ PERMETTANT DE RÉALISER UN ACCÈS ALÉATOIRE DANS UN SYSTÈME DE COMMUNICATION SANS FIL</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">APPARATUS AND METHOD FOR PERFORMING RANDOM ACCESS IN WIRELESS COMMUNICATION SYSTEM</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A wireless device (900) comprises a radio frequency unit; a memory; and a processor. The processor is configured to cause the wireless device (900) to transmit, to a base station (950), a first random access preamble; determine, based on a transmission time point associated with the first random access preamble, a time window for monitoring for a random access response; receive, during the time window, a first random access response; prepare, based on the first random access response not including response information for the wireless device, for a random access preamble retransmission, and perform, based on the preparation, the random access preamble retransmission. When preparing the random access preamble retransmission a time for the preparation is set based on one of a first subcarrier spacing associated with the first random access preamble; or a second subcarrier spacing associated with the first random access response.</p>
            </abstract>
